From bbd1095a971f41d66a37c8a298bbe1f6adb46710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:44:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ci(fork): run CI on fork-rebuild and publish a release for
 every green push

CI only ran on main pushes, so fork-rebuild never got checked. It now also
runs on fork-rebuild pushes, and once every job passes, ci.yml calls the
fork-release workflow. That workflow cross-compiles engram for five platforms,
packs the Pi plugin, writes checksums and publishes a GitHub release tagged
fork-YYYY.MM.DD.N.

The notes come from scripts/fork-release.sh. They list the commits since the
previous fork release (or, after a route-B rebuild, the patches added and
removed) and the full patch series, using the Chinese titles from the
docs/fork-patches table. The fork- prefix keeps upstream's v* release, image
and Pi publishing workflows from firing. A commit that already has a fork tag
is skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
